# Workspace-root .dockerignore.
#
# It lives here rather than in the product directory because the build context
# is now the workspace root:
#   docker build -f apps/website-builder/Dockerfile -t landingos-builder .
# Docker only ever reads the .dockerignore at the context root, so a file left
# inside apps/website-builder/ would be silently ignored and every excluded
# path would ship in the image.

# Build artifacts — regenerated inside the image
**/.next
.git
**/.gitignore

# Generated Prisma clients — ALWAYS regenerated in the builder stage, so the
# query engines match the image's platform (linux-musl), never a dev machine's.
# A dev-machine client in the context is dead weight at best and, if the
# generate step were ever skipped, a windows .dll shipping to Linux at worst.
packages/db/prisma/client
apps/website-builder/src/generated

# Local deps + data — never bake these into the image
**/node_modules
**/db/*.db
**/db/*.db-journal
**/data

# ERP runtime database, in every form it takes
**/crm.db
**/crm.db-wal
**/crm.db-shm

# Local dev files
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.log
**/dev-out.log
**/dev-err.log

# OS / editor noise
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Local-only tooling that shouldn't ship
**/.local-preview
**/.zscripts
**/bun.lock
**/.claude
